Apache NiFi

This product is built on and derived from Apache NiFi
(https://nifi.apache.org/), Copyright The Apache Software Foundation,
licensed under the Apache License 2.0.

This product includes software developed at
The Apache Software Foundation (http://www.apache.org/).

The derivation takes three forms:

1. Derived source code.
   Several extension bundles under `nifi-extensions/` contain source files
   originally taken from Apache NiFi 1.28.0 (tag `rel/nifi-1.28.0`) and adapted
   for Apache NiFi 2.10. Those files retain the original ASF license header and
   carry an additional notice identifying the upstream file they were derived
   from, as required by sections 4(b) and 4(c) of the Apache License 2.0.
   The affected bundles are:

     nifi-argus-standard-bundle              from nifi-standard-bundle
     nifi-argus-db-bundle                    from nifi-standard-bundle,
                                                  nifi-extension-utils
     nifi-argus-hive-bundle                  from nifi-hive-bundle (Hive 3)
     nifi-argus-kudu-bundle                  from nifi-kudu-bundle
     nifi-argus-parquet-bundle               from nifi-parquet-bundle,
                                                  nifi-extension-utils
     nifi-argus-record-serialization-bundle  from nifi-record-serialization-
                                                  services-bundle
     nifi-argus-reporting-bundle             from nifi-standard-bundle
                                                  (standard reporting tasks)
     nifi-argus-iceberg-bundle               from nifi-iceberg-bundle

   Each NAR module carries the NOTICE of the upstream bundle it derives from,
   under `src/main/resources/META-INF/NOTICE`.

   The following bundles are original works of Data Dynamics Inc. and are not
   derived from Apache NiFi source: nifi-argus-debezium-bundle,
   nifi-argus-deltalake-bundle, nifi-argus-flow-analysis-bundle.

2. Redistributed binaries.
   The `distribution/` module repackages the official Apache NiFi 2.10.0 binary
   distribution together with the Argus NAR extensions and a configuration
   overlay, producing tar.gz and RPM artifacts. Those artifacts contain Apache
   NiFi in unmodified binary form, along with its own LICENSE and NOTICE files.

3. Container images.
   The image built from `docker/Dockerfile` uses the official `apache/nifi`
   image as its base and adds the Argus NAR extensions. The base image is
   redistributed unmodified under its own license terms.

